in', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.io.formatoptions', 'qualified_name': 'ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'kind': 'function', 'name': 'write_espresso_in', 'class': None, 'function': 'write_espresso_in', 'chunk_index': 2, 'num_chunks': 5}, 'score': 2.6177194118499756, 'vector_score': 0.614861786365509, 'bm25_score': 20.34282318602198, 'rerank_score': 2.6177194118499756}, {'text': "[ase.calculators.espresso.Espresso]\ninput_data: dict A flat or nested dictionary with input parameters for pw.x pseudopotentials: dict A filename for each atomic species, e.g. {'O': 'O.pbe-rrkjus.UPF', 'H': 'H.pbe-rrkjus.UPF'} . A dummy name will be used if none are given. kspacing: float Generate a grid of k-points with this as the minimum distance,\nin A^-1 between them in reciprocal space. If set to None, kpts\nwill be used instead. kpts: (int, int, int), dict, or BandPath If kpts is a tuple (or list) of 3 integers, it is interpreted\nas the dimensions of a Monkhorst-Pack grid. If kpts is set to None , only the Γ-point will be included\nand QE will use routines optimized for Γ-point-only calculations. Compared to Γ-point-only calculations without this optimization\n(i.e. with kpts=(1, 1, 1) ), the memory and CPU requirements\nare typically reduced by half.", 'title': 'ase.calculators.espresso.Espresso', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/calculators/espresso.html#ase.calculators.espresso.Espresso', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.calculators.espresso', 'qualified_name': 'ase.calculators.espresso.Espresso', 'kind': 'class', 'name': 'Espresso', 'class': 'Espresso', 'chunk_index': 1, 'num_chunks': 3}, 'score': 1.9338339567184448, 'vector_score': 0.47241052985191345, 'bm25_score': 14.56446346024219, 'rerank_score': 1.9338339567184448}, {'text': '[ase.calculators.espresso.Espresso]\nIf kpts is a dict, it will either be interpreted as a path\nin the Brillouin zone (*) if it contains the ‘path’ keyword,\notherwise it is converted to a Monkhorst-Pack grid (**). (*) see ase.dft.kpoints.bandpath\n(**) see ase.calculators.calculator.kpts2sizeandoffsets koffset: (int, int, int) Offset of kpoints in each direction. Must be 0 (no offset) or\n1 (half grid offset). Setting to True is equivalent to (1, 1, 1).', 'title': 'ase.calculators.espresso.Espresso', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/calculators/espresso.html#ase.calculators.espresso.Espresso', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.calculators.espresso', 'qualified_name': 'ase.calculators.espresso.Espresso', 'kind': 'class', 'name': 'Espresso', 'class': 'Espresso', 'chunk_index': 2, 'num_chunks': 3}, 'score': 1.83260977268219, 'vector_score': 0.5247504711151123, 'bm25_score': None, 'rerank_score': 1.83260977268219}]}

